#!/usr/bin/env bash
# zdev-worker-prompt <RepoName> <bead-id> [extra context...]: emit a full worker dispatch prompt
set -euo pipefail
R="${1:?usage: zdev-worker-prompt <RepoName> <bead-id> [context]}"
B="${2:?bead id required}"
shift 2 || true
EXTRA="${*:-}"
D="$HOME/AI/$R"
cd "$D"
SHOW=$(br show "$B")
cat <<EOF
You are working ONLY on $R at $D. Complete exactly one bead: $B. Run \`br show $B\` for full context. Bead summary:

$SHOW

STRICT SCOPE RULES:
- Do NOT touch any file outside $D.
- NEVER run destructive commands: no rm -rf, no git clean, no git reset --hard, no git checkout ., no mass deletions.
- Do NOT run full test suites. Targeted tests only for code you changed; default verification is cargo check (or the repo's cheapest check).
- Do NOT refactor unrelated code. Max 2 retries on any failing command; if stuck twice, record findings in bead notes (br update $B --notes) and stop.

EFFICIENCY RULES (target: <=3 tool calls for a typical bead — see docs/worker-loop-efficiency.md):
- BATCH. One plan is a JS program: put find + read + edit + verify + revert in a SINGLE tool call. Extra zero.fs.compound/zero.token.shell actions inside one plan are free. Split only when a later step's content depends on what you just read.
- Chain shell steps with && inside one shell action; merge reads (sed -n 'A,Bp;C,Dp'); return refs and short summaries, not whole files.
- PREWARM the compiler once (cargo test -p <crate> --no-run, or cargo check) in your first plan, then each verify is link-and-run instead of a full rebuild.
- Reuse the shared target/ dir (you are the only writer for this repo this wave). Do NOT set CARGO_TARGET_DIR — a fresh target dir is a guaranteed cold build.
- Scope every verify: cargo test -p <crate> --lib <filter>. Never a full suite.
$EXTRA

DELIVERY: commit with clear messages; \`br close $B --reason "<evidence: test names + how you mutation-verified>"\` ONLY if acceptance is proved, else \`br update $B --notes "<findings>"\` leaving in_progress. Then \`br sync --flush-only\`. Report: files changed, commits, test commands + results, bead status.
EOF
